Hello,

We have recently upgraded our Kafka brokers to version 4.0.0 and have noticed that our latencies are substantially worse than on 3.9.1 (both versions running with KRaft).

We have created a small project that demonstrates the issue. It has a single producer and consumer and measures how long it takes between the producer sending the record and the consumer pulling it off (both clients are using version 3.9.1 in the experiments). A record is sent every millisecond.
Below are the results:

Kafka 3.9.1

50th percentile:     297 us
90th percentile:     366 us
99th percentile:     528 us
99.9th percentile: 1,460 us

Kafka 4.0.0

50th percentile:    8,178 us
90th percentile:   10,355 us
99th percentile:   11,042 us
99.9th percentile: 13,638 us

Kafka has been started locally in a docker container using `docker run -p 9092:9092 project/kafka:3.9.1` and then `docker run -p 9092:9092 project/kafka:4.0.0`.

